{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/792068-where-do-i-find-the-rules-about-resources-6-and-the-relationship-map","id":792068,"title":"Where do I find the rules about Resources 6+? And the \"relationship map\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-24T02:52:38-08:00","id":792068,"title":"Where do I find the rules about Resources 6+? And the \"relationship map\"?","content":"I've been going through my VtR 1E PDFs, trying to find a couple game systems, but I canNOT find them.<br /> <br /> <b>Resources</b><br /> This system was for representing characters with fantastic Resources, of six or more dotes. I remember it being a fun read. Don't know whether I'd ever actually <i>use </i>it, mind you.<br /> <br /> <b>Relationships</b><br /> This was a system for creating relationships between characters during character creation, and then during play. It encompassed not just the player characters, but also NPCs and locations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:22:03-08:00","id":792079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/792068-where-do-i-find-the-rules-about-resources-6-and-the-relationship-map#post792068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Resources</b><br /> This system was for representing characters with fantastic Resources, of six or more dotes. I remember it being a fun read. Don't know whether I'd ever actually <i>use </i>it, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two different systems for this. One is in Damnation City, on page 234, and hooks into the Primacy mechanics. Another is in the Chroniclers Guide, on page 68.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/792068-where-do-i-find-the-rules-about-resources-6-and-the-relationship-map#post792068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Relationships</b><br /> This was a system for creating relationships between characters during character creation, and then during play. It encompassed not just the player characters, but also NPCs and locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about this one. I know there is a relationship creation system in VtR 2nd edition, but you were expressly asking about first edition systems.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:33:19-08:00","id":792083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Resources</b><br /> This system was for representing characters with fantastic Resources, of six or more dotes. I remember it being a fun read. Don't know whether I'd ever actually <i>use </i>it, mind you. </div> </div> </div>That sounds like Damnation City. Or at least there are mechanics for making that the focus of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T05:05:26-08:00","id":792105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/792068-where-do-i-find-the-rules-about-resources-6-and-the-relationship-map#post792068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Relationships</b><br /> This was a system for creating relationships between characters during character creation, and then during play. It encompassed not just the player characters, but also NPCs and locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not certain, but this could be Hell Is Other People from The Danse Macabre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T06:58:46-08:00","id":792157,"title":"","content":"I believe Mirrors had systems for Rapport and Pc connections, Seers of the Throne has the Luxury Merit, which is on way to model Resources 6+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T09:06:33-08:00","id":792209,"title":"","content":"The relationships thing could be the Climbing the Ladder section, from second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T11:37:49-08:00","id":792273,"title":"","content":"I checked <b>Damnation City</b>. It's on point, but it's not the passage I was looking for.<br /> <br /> I recall the passage had an example, and a drawing. I recall the drawing reminded me of a board room set in the Middle East. I believe one of the characters (an ancient Middle-Eastern Nosferatu?) has Resources 8, and the example demonstrated how he could block a team-up between two vampires who had resources 6 and 7.<br /> <br /> I think it also had examples of what you could &quot;buy&quot; with each level of Resources.<br /> <br /> I'm not making a judgment on whether the system was good. Just would like to reread it.<br /> <br /> As for <b>Hell is Other People</b>... awesome! I don't think it's what I was looking for, but I'll probably use that at some point.<br /> <br /> The Relationships system I was thinking of reminded me of a similar system from <b>Cortex Plus Drama </b>(originally presented in the <b>Smallville </b>RPG), where every player would create a location or character, and then another player could create something, draw a connection to something, or establish something about that connection. It's a neat way to get the ball rolling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:44:19-08:00","id":792312,"title":"","content":"The example for the Resources thing you're talking about is from the Vampire the Requiem Chronicler's Guide, p69.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:06:45-08:00","id":792322,"title":"","content":"Oh, thanks, nofather! That was definitely it.<br /> I love that drawing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:45:32-08:00","id":792473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/792068-where-do-i-find-the-rules-about-resources-6-and-the-relationship-map?p=792273#post792273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Relationships system I was thinking of reminded me of a similar system from <b>Cortex Plus Drama </b>(originally presented in the <b>Smallville </b>RPG), where every player would create a location or character, and then another player could create something, draw a connection to something, or establish something about that connection. It's a neat way to get the ball rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely Climbing the Ladder. Requiem Second Edition, pages 282 to 287.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T00:04:43-08:00","id":792636,"title":"","content":"Awesome!<br /> <br /> I could have sworn I saw a similar system before 2nd Edition came out. Must just be a mistaken memory.<br /> <br /> Regardless, glad to know!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T12:03:03-08:00","id":793220,"title":"","content":"God Machine Chronicle also has very similar system for creating a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T09:17:37-08:00","id":798287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/792068-where-do-i-find-the-rules-about-resources-6-and-the-relationship-map#post792068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Relationships</b><br /> This was a system for creating relationships between characters during character creation, and then during play. It encompassed not just the player characters, but also NPCs and locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I think you might be remembering (at least, it's the first thing that popped into my head when I read this) was a blog post by David Hill about it, some time ago. Sadly, if I recall properly, his blog got eaten by a server somewhere and the blog post was lost. Which is sad because when I've used that approach, the players loved it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T13:13:16-08:00","id":798365,"title":"","content":"Could be!<br /> <br /> The relation map from VtR 2E is definitely pretty cool, but I tried looking this up a while ago, before that book came out.<br /> <br /> It's not a <i>big </i>deal, but I liked referencing CofD material instead of drag+and+dropping Smallville. I suppose it's easy enough to just use the Cortex+Drama system, or check out that VtR 2E entry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}